The lead's item from fix-data-6 (2026-10-24): naming places made the card's pill three or four lines at every VISIBLE
size. It keeps BP-2's 10.5em where the whole sentence fits two lines, widens to 15.5em where it doesn't (under the title on
a phone), and only past that shows a shorter form (one place named, "For … only", "Posted for other places"); the
card's accessible name and the tip keep the whole sentence. D-15 over VISIBLE and TABLETS: 31 of 31 fail before, 31
pass after. fix-viz-5's V-46 looped over all 31 sizes in one test and ran past the harness's 120 s: one test for the
phones and postures, one for the iPads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
