+22. **D-15, the "Pay posted for … only" pill** (the lead, 2026-10-24, from fix-data-6, whose P-1 names the places): at
+    10.5em it took 3 lines for two places and 4 for "Santa Clara, Sunnyvale and 3 more" at all 21 VISIBLE sizes (at 280 and
+    320 px under the title, still 137 px wide). Tried on six postings at six sizes: 14em leaves 3 lines for the longest,
+    15.5em gives 2 everywhere; widening every such pill made "Pay posted for Tempe only" one line and squeezed its title to 5
+    lines at 375 px. So the pill keeps 10.5em where the whole sentence fits two lines and widens only where it doesn't
+    (`fitPill`, measured, `.is-wide`); the shorter forms (one place named, fix-data-6's "For … only" and "Posted for other
+    places") come only past that. With 15.5em the whole sentence fits two lines at every VISIBLE size for all six, 280 and
+    320 px included, so those show it whole rather than fix-data-6's short form; the short forms stay for longer lists. The
+    card's accessible name and the tip keep the whole sentence.
+23. **On the new base (fix-data-6's 217ff5c)**: the D commits cherry-picked cleanly. Two related failures on the f13ebd6
+    run were the size patch's, not the folding: fix-viz-5's V-46 loops over ALL_SIZES in one test and ran past the
+    harness's 120 s with the iPads (74 s with 21 sizes before), so it is two tests, phones and postures, then tablets; Fix
+    touch tips at 834x1084 (a new TABLETS size) tapped a 2 px strip bar whose touch lands on the axis under it (the
+    one-row top bar moved the strip to a half pixel), which qa-ci-6's a5bdbc9 fixes by tapping the tallest bars first.
 
